From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tom <tompt@seznam.cz>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:45:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: iio: light: describe CT709 factory calibration

The bootloader passes the per-unit dual-sensor record at the aliased node. Describe the resolved byte array, including the padding present on J120.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: tom <tompt@seznam.cz>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/iio/light/apple,ct709.yaml     | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/light/apple,ct709.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/light/apple,ct709.yaml
index 5a91701fd..59a918861 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/light/apple,ct709.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/light/apple,ct709.yaml
@@ -20,6 +20,16 @@ properties:
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  apple,als-calibration:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint8-array
+    minItems: 6696
+    maxItems: 9992
+    description:
+      Factory calibration supplied by the bootloader from the resolved Apple
+      device tree alsCalibration property. On J120 the eight-byte header and
+      two 3344-byte orientation records can be followed by padding. The
+      property on the als0 node contains records for both sensors.
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
